{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under **SEC Rule 22c-1**, the ETF’s **board of directors or trustees** sets the specific time or times for calculating NAV, in its discretion.\n\nNAV must generally be computed **at least once daily, Monday through Friday**, subject to the rule’s limited exceptions—not merely whenever an authorized participant places an order.\n\n**4 p.m. Eastern is the usual convention**, tied to the NYSE’s regular trading close; it is **not a universally mandated SEC pricing time**. A fund can use another properly established and disclosed time. Treatment of early market closes depends on the fund’s policy and disclosures.\n\nAn ETF’s intraday exchange trading does not itself require intraday official NAV calculations."}}
